 "tourapi_codes_about": "TourAPI areacode (the older area codes) and lDongRegnCd (the legal-dong province code of KorService2) are kept apart: code 31 is Gyeonggi as an areacode and Ulsan as an lDongRegnCd. A code is used only when the address (addr1) does not name a different region; an unknown code falls back to the address.",
  "about_search": "Korean items of Wikidata found by a full-text search (CirrusSearch, haswbstatement:P17=Q884) of named things: labels, descriptions and aliases in any language. A hit becomes a project only when the entity rules accept it, it is located in Korea and it has a place, venue, event or work class (review/korea.json search.decisions).",
  "search_terms": ["빛축제", "빛 축제", "빛초롱", "유등축제", "루미나리에", "불빛축제", "미디어아트", "미디어 아트", "미디어파사드", "미디어 파사드", "프로젝션 매핑", "라이트쇼", "몰입형", "야간경관", "빛의 벙커", "아르떼뮤지엄", "light festival", "lantern festival", "media art", "media facade"],
  "about_label_scan": "Full-text search splits no Korean compounds (\"유등축제\" never finds \"진주남강유등축제\"), so one SPARQL query also reads the Korean labels of the items in Korea (wdt:P17 wd:Q884) that contain one of these terms (#aol:kr-label-scan, at most label_scan_limit rows). A hit goes through the same gates as a search hit (entity rules, located in Korea, a place, event or work class).",
